+/*
+ * How long a task will spin for its own reply before going to sleep.
+ *
+ * A synchronous FUSE request costs far more to deliver than the server takes
+ * to answer it. The reply lands in the used ring, the device raises an
+ * interrupt, the handler schedules a work item, the workqueue thread runs and
+ * ends the request, and only then is the waiting task woken — two trips
+ * through the scheduler for work that finished microseconds ago.
+ *
+ * Spinning instead skips all of it: the submitting task drains its own reply
+ * in its own context, so nothing is scheduled and nothing is woken.
+ *
+ * How long to spin depends on what the other end is doing, and there are two
+ * regimes. With the device relying on the notification register, the trap the
+ * driver takes to ring it is also a rendezvous: the host answers inside the
+ * trap, so the reply is already there when the write retires and ten
+ * microseconds is plenty. Spinning longer than that only takes a core away
+ * from the work that would have filled the ring, and at two milliseconds it is
+ * twice as slow as not polling at all.
+ *
+ * With a device that watches the ring instead, there is no trap and so no
+ * rendezvous: a reply that arrives after the spin gives up costs an interrupt
+ * and a wake-up, which is dearer than the trap that was removed. The spin then
+ * has to cover the operation rather than the delivery, and a create on APFS is
+ * twenty-five microseconds of it. Measured against such a device the curve
+ * bottoms out at a hundred: create-and-close falls from 50.3 microseconds to
+ * 35.3, and a four-kilobyte write from 60.6 to 45.7. Thirty is most of the
+ * win and three hundred is no better.
+ *
+ * Zero disables it, and `virtiofs.poll_usecs=` on the kernel command line
+ * changes it, so the trade can be re-measured without rebuilding anything.
+ * The module is `virtiofs` and not `virtio_fs`; getting that wrong silently
+ * leaves the default in place and makes an A/B compare a value with itself.
+ */
+static unsigned int poll_usecs = 100;
+module_param_named(poll_usecs, poll_usecs, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(poll_usecs,
+		 "microseconds to spin for a reply before sleeping (0 disables)");
+
